From: =?UTF-8?q?Yusuf=20=C4=B0hsan=20KILIN=C3=87?= <78423442+yusufklncc@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 05:25:05 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] intel: add -Dintel-internal-shaders=stub to build anv
 without mesa-clc and glslang

anv's internal shaders (indirect draw generation, query copies, DGC, the
resinfo helpers, blorp's indirect copies) are OpenCL C compiled by
mesa-clc, which needs LLVM, and the fp64 library, BVH builders and ASTC
decoder are GLSL compiled by glslang. Neither is available on every
host (macOS without Homebrew), which makes it impossible to bring anv
up there at all.

With intel-internal-shaders=stub the intel Vulkan driver no longer pulls
in mesa-clc or glslang: ray tracing is off, the generated NIR builders are
replaced by stubs that log and abort when used, blorp keeps a hand-written
blorp_check_in_bounds(), and ASTC emulation and the runtime's BVH helpers
are compiled out. Meant for bring-up only; the default stays 'enabled'.

Generated-by: LLM
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
